  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing due to filesystem permissions on uploads directory \u2014 not disk or database.\n\n**Root cause:** host directory `/srv/lab-data/uploads` (`/data/uploads` in container) is not writable by the application user.\n\n* App container runs as `1000:1000` (E6) with bind `source: /srv/lab-data -> destination: /data, rw: true` (E6).\n* Host path `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `owner_uid: 0, owner_gid: 0, mode: 0755` with `app_uid: 1000, app_user_can_write: false` (E4).\n* Parent `/srv/lab-data` is `owner_uid: 1000, owner_gid: 1000` with `app_user_can_write: true` (E10), so problem is specific to `uploads/` ownership, not parent or mount read-only.\n* Effective failure confirmed, not just mode-bit inference (E4 method ignores ACLs): app log shows `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/...part' -> '/data/uploads/...'` on `POST /upload` -> `500 Internal Server Error` (E5) and `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health-...'` on health probe in `main.py:116 health` (E5).\n\n**Symptoms:**\n* `POST /upload 500` then `GET /health 503` in app logs (E5).\n* External health `http://localhost:8080/health status_code: 503 body: {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2) while containers `incidentlab-app-1 running Up 5 seconds, incidentlab-db-1 running Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1).\n\n**Ruled out:**\n* Disk/inode full: `/srv/lab-data use_percent: 9.0 inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E3) and `/ use_percent: 6.8 inode_use_percent: 1.5` (E11).\n* Read-only mount: mount `rw: true` (E6).\n* Database dependency: `incidentlab-db-1 healthy` (E1), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` (E8), inspect `running: true, health: healthy, oom_killed: false` (E9), recent events `health_status: healthy` and `exec_die exit 0` for `pg_isready` (E7).\n* Crash/OOM of app: `running: true, exit_code: 0, oom_killed: false` (E6).\n\nRepair requires host-side `chown 1000:1000 /srv/lab-data/uploads` / permission fix \u2014 separate approval, not done here.\n",
